{"source_id":"W2593975868","title":"An Investigation of Note-Taking and Review on Test Performance","year":2016,"abstract":"Note-taking is a ubiquitous behavior among students, yet its function remains debated. The present study examined the effects of note-taking medium (longhand vs. laptop) and note review on test performance. Participants viewed a lecture and took notes either longhand or by laptop, then either reviewed their notes or did not review before completing a test of factual and conceptual questions. Results indicated a main effect of review, such that participants who reviewed notes performed better than those who did not, but no significant interaction between note-taking medium and review was found. Longhand note takers did not outperform laptop note takers on conceptual questions, and the benefit of review was similar across medium conditions."}
